# Try the API from your IDE: Visual Studio, VS Code (REST Client extension) or Rider.
# Start Postgres and the API first (`docker compose up -d`, then `dotnet run`).
# Run "Log in" first: later requests reuse its token via {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5133

### Log in as the demo user (created in Development only; see appsettings.Development.json)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@example.com", "password": "Demo123!" }

### Who am I?
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### List my todos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create a todo (also pushes "todo-changed" to your open browser tabs over SignalR)
# @name createTodo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Try Wolverine" }

### Remind me about the todo in a minute (a scheduled Wolverine message; it arrives in open browser tabs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/{{createTodo.response.body.$.id}}/remind
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "minutes": 1 }

### Complete the todo created above (cascades TodoCompleted to a background handler; see the API log)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todos/{{createTodo.response.body.$.id}}/complete
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Validation: an empty title is rejected with 400 and ProblemDetails
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "" }

### Update your profile. A new email (also the login name) is used only after the link
### emailed to it is opened (in Development, see Mailpit: http://localhost:8025)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/account/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@example.com", "displayName": "Demo User" }

### Ask for a password reset email (in Development, read it in Mailpit: http://localhost:8025)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@example.com" }

### Admin: list users (the demo user is an admin in Development; others get 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users?search=example
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

#if (Saas)
### My organisations (isCurrent: the one my access token is for)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/organisations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The current organisation, and my role in it
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/organisation
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Its members
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/organisation/members
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Invite someone to it (the email lands in Mailpit: http://localhost:8025)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/organisation/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "teammate@example.com", "role": "Member" }

### Create another organisation (I'm its owner)
# @name createOrganisation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/organisations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Another team" }

### Switch to it: new tokens for the same session (its Todos are separate). This replaces the
### login's refresh token, so run "Log in" again before the requests below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/organisations/switch
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "organisationId": "{{createOrganisation.response.body.$.id}}", "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

#endif
### Without a token, the Todo endpoints answer 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/todos

### Get a new access token (the refresh token rotates: the old one stops working)
# @name refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### Log out (revokes the refresh token from the latest refresh)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refresh.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }
